# Gargoylite

## Lore

Gargoylites are a comparatively tiny, squat version of the gargoyle lords, and may be further evidence of the gargoyle''s strange evolution. Physically they are unimposing: three feet tall, with round pudgy bodies, stumpy legs and small, seemingly underdeveloped wings. Their skin is green, their horns tiny, their eyes yellow-orange, and their short tail is ineffectual in battle.

As for instinct, gargoylites do not share the aggressiveness and joy of combat of their larger kin. They tend toward mischief, thievery, deception and manipulation rather than wholesale destruction. They also lack the lust for power and the need to dominate others - but they are obsessive and psychotically greedy for precious and semi-precious stones.

Their deceptive nature has made them the favourite spies of gargoyle lords and mages. Shifters, summoners and other powerful beings have also found gargoylites to be wonderful spies and allies.

## GM Notes

The average NPC gargoylite ranges from 1D4+1 levels, but can be virtually any level. Gargoylites of high level - ninth and higher - are often revered and envied by other gargoylites as master thieves and spies, and are likely to command a pack of 3D4 gargoylite thieves and a dozen gurgoyles or other lesser minions.

Gargoylites are one of the gargoyle mage''s favourite minions, used for reconnaissance, spying, theft and assassination.

Their short, stubby little wings appear useless but can carry the gargoylite and up to 500 pounds with ease. They cannot sustain long flights - thirty minutes at most - and must take frequent rests or hitch a ride.

Habitat is the same as the gargoyle''s. Everything else about how Europeans treat these creatures is the common Gargoyle''s; see that class.
